<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Zayd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 900</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn Zayd was the second ruler of the Alavid (Zaydi) state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>, succeeding his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-zayd">Hasan ibn Zayd</a> in 884. Governing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amol">Amol</a> with the support of Daylamite warriors, he held the Caspian lands against rivals and Abbasid governors. In 900 he invaded Khurasan and was defeated and killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorgan">Gorgan</a>, ending the first Alavid state.</p></div>
